    "id": "thm:latent-dimension",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every \\((G,P)\\in\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{cert}}^{(q)}(K,J)\\), \\(\\operatorname{rank}(T_{12})=q^K\\), and consequently \\(K_{\\min}(P_X)=K\\) even when a competing realization with fewer \\(q\\)-state coordinates is not double triangular.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "G",
      "P",
      "q",
      "K",
      "J",
      "\\(\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm{cert}}^{(q)}(K,J)\\)",
      "\\(T_{12}\\)",
      "\\(K_{\\min}\\)",
      "\\(P_X\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:positive-support",
      "ass:certificate",
      "def:certified-class",
      "thm:certificate-frontier"
    ],
    "justification": "The latent dimension becomes a functional of the observed law rather than analyst input.",
    "gap": "Lee and Gu (2026, Theorem 1) prove the binary rank exclusion; Kivva et al. (2021) obtain component orders from a mixture oracle.",
    "consumer": "It selects the number of polytomous skills before model fitting.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(r=q^K\\). Membership in the certified class, Assumption~\\textnormal{ass:certificate}, and Theorem~\\textnormal{thm:certificate-frontier} imply that \\(M_1\\) and \\(M_2\\) are invertible. Assumption~\\textnormal{ass:positive-support} makes every diagonal entry of \\(\\operatorname{diag}(\\pi)\\) positive. Therefore\n\\[\n T_{12}=M_1\\operatorname{diag}(\\pi)M_2^{\\mathsf T}\n\\]\nis a product of three invertible \\(r\\times r\\) matrices, and\n\\[\n \\operatorname{rank}(T_{12})=r=q^K.\n\\]\n\nNow consider any \\(q\\)-state measurement-model realization of the same observed law with \\(L\\) latent coordinates. Conditional independence of observed vertices given the complete latent vector gives a factorization of the same two-view matrix as\n\\[\n T_{12}=\\widetilde M_1\\operatorname{diag}(\\widetilde\\pi)\n \\widetilde M_2^{\\mathsf T},\n\\]\nwhere each \\(\\widetilde M_a\\) has \\(q^L\\) columns. Hence\n\\[\n q^K=\\operatorname{rank}(T_{12})\\le q^L.\n\\]\nBecause \\(q\\ge3>1\\), this inequality implies \\(L\\ge K\\). The original realization shows \\(K_{\\min}(P_X)\\le K\\), while the rank argument gives \\(K_{\\min}(P_X)\\ge K\\). Thus \\(K_{\\min}(P_X)=K\\). The competing realization was used only through its measurement-model factorization, so no triangularity or certificate was imposed on it.",
